[Term]
id: FMA:7490
name: Joint
namespace: fma
def: "Heterogeneous cluster which consists of two or more adjacent bones or cartilages, parts of  which are interconnected by organ parts that consist of various types of connective tissue. Together with other joints and bones, a joint constitutes the skeletal system. Examples: pubic symphysis, knee joint, temporomandibular joint." []
is_a: FMA:62955 ! Anatomical entity
is_a: PROMOT:7000001 ! Phenotypically related anatomical entity

[Term]
id: FMA:7491
name: Nonsynovial joint
namespace: fma
def: "Joint in which the articulating bones or cartilages are connected by ligaments or fibrocartilage without an intervening synovial cavity. Examples: sagittal suture, inferior tibiofibular syndesmosis, costochondral joint, pubic symphysis." []
synonym: "Solid joint" EXACT []
is_a: FMA:7490 ! Joint

[Term]
id: FMA:7492
name: Fibrous joint
namespace: fma
def: "Nonsynovial joint in which the articulating bones or cartilages are connected by ligaments. Examples: sagittal suture, inferior tibiofibular syndesmosis, gomphosis." []
synonym: "Articulatio fibrosa" EXACT []
is_a: FMA:7491 ! Nonsynovial joint

[Term]
id: FMA:7493
name: Suture
namespace: fma
def: "Fibrous joint in which the articulating bones or cartilages of the skull are connected by sutural ligaments (scant amount of collagenous dense connective tissue). Examples: sagittal suture, frontal suture." []
is_a: FMA:7492 ! Fibrous joint

[Term]
id: FMA:7494
name: Syndesmosis
namespace: fma
def: "Fibrous joint in which the articulating bones or cartilages of the vertebral column and the limbs as well as articulating ossicles, are connected by skeletal ligaments or membranes. Examples: Intervertebral syndesmosis, inferior tibiofibular joint." []
is_a: FMA:7492 ! Fibrous joint

[Term]
id: FMA:7495
name: Dento-alveolar joint
namespace: fma
def: "Fibrous joint in which the periodontal ligament connects a tooth to the alveolar bone of the maxilla or mandible. Examples: Dento-alveolar joint of incisor tooth." []
synonym: "Dento-alveolar syndesmosis" EXACT []
synonym: "Peg-and-socket joint" EXACT []
synonym: "Socket" EXACT []
is_a: FMA:7492 ! Fibrous joint

[Term]
id: FMA:7496
name: Cartilaginous joint
namespace: fma
def: "Nonsynovial joint in which the articulating bones or cartilages are connected by cartilage. Examples: Spheno-occipital synchondrosis, first sternocostal joint, pubic symphysis." []
synonym: "Articulatio cartilaginea" EXACT []
is_a: FMA:7491 ! Nonsynovial joint

[Term]
id: FMA:7497
name: Synchondrosis
namespace: fma
def: "Cartilaginous joint in which the articulating bones or cartilages are connected by hyaline cartilage. Examples: spheno-occipital synchondrosis, first sternocostal joint." []
synonym: "Epiphysial cartilage" EXACT []
synonym: "Primary cartilaginous joint" EXACT []
is_a: FMA:7496 ! Cartilaginous joint

[Term]
id: FMA:7498
name: Symphysis
namespace: fma
def: "Cartilaginous joint in which the articulating bones or cartilages are connected by fibrocartilage. Examples: pubic symphysis, intervertebral symphysis, manubriosternal joint." []
synonym: "Secondary cartilaginous joint" EXACT []
is_a: FMA:7496 ! Cartilaginous joint

[Term]
id: FMA:7499
name: Synostosis
namespace: fma
def: "Nonsynovial joint in which the articulating bones are connected by bone. Examples: epiphyseal junction, manubriosternal synostosis." []
synonym: "Bony union" EXACT []
is_a: FMA:7491 ! Nonsynovial joint

[Term]
id: FMA:7501
name: Synovial joint
namespace: fma
def: "Joint in which the articulating bones or cartilages are connected by an articular capsule which encloses a synovial membrane and a synovial cavity. Examples: Temporomandibular joint, knee joint." []
synonym: "Articulatio synoviale" EXACT []
is_a: FMA:7490 ! Joint

[Term]
id: FMA:7502
name: Manubriosternal joint
namespace: fma
synonym: "Manubriosternal symphysis" EXACT []
is_a: FMA:7498 ! Symphysis

[Term]
id: FMA:7503
name: Xiphisternal joint
namespace: fma
synonym: "Synchondrosis xiphisternalis" EXACT []
is_a: FMA:7498 ! Symphysis

